WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.334 --> 00:00:17.400
While the Darling family was happily hugging upstairs, the Lost Boys were waiting outside.

2
00:00:17.401 --> 00:00:25.667
Wendy needed time to tell her parents about them, so the boys counted to five hundred before knocking on the front door.

3
00:00:25.668 --> 00:00:30.296
They thought this was more polite than flying through the window.

4
00:00:30.297 --> 00:00:37.552
When Mr. and Mrs. Darling opened the door, the boys stood in a row, looking as innocent as they could.

5
00:00:37.553 --> 00:00:42.731
Each had a sweet grin on his face and an eager spark in his eyes.

6
00:00:42.732 --> 00:00:48.327
"We are very pleased to meet you," the boys said together.

7
00:00:48.328 --> 00:00:54.443
All their attention was on Mrs. Darling, for they hoped she would be their new mother.

8
00:00:54.444 --> 00:00:58.425
Of course she told the boys right away that she would adopt them.

9
00:00:58.426 --> 00:01:01.818
But Mr. Darling did not feel quite the same way.

10
00:01:01.819 --> 00:01:07.351
"Six new children is an awfully large number," he said, worried.

11
00:01:07.352 --> 00:01:10.216
"It will be very expensive."

12
00:01:10.217 --> 00:01:16.574
"George!" Mrs. Darling cried, upset to see his selfishness come out again.

13
00:01:16.575 --> 00:01:22.659
Then Mr. Darling burst into a smile. He was as glad to have them as she was.

14
00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:28.200
"I just thought you could have asked my permission," he said.

15
00:01:28.201 --> 00:01:33.364
The boys all told him that having a father was just as important as having a mother.

16
00:01:33.365 --> 00:01:38.790
Delighted, Mr. Darling said that he would find space for them in an extra room.

17
00:01:38.791 --> 00:01:44.532
"We can all fit into a single bed, sir," Tootles assured him.

18
00:01:44.533 --> 00:01:49.308
"Then follow me," Mr. Darling cried merrily.

19
00:01:49.309 --> 00:01:55.037
"Mind you, I'm not sure that we have an extra room, but we can pretend to have one."

20
00:01:55.038 --> 00:01:59.633
He went off dancing through the house, and the boys danced after him.

21
00:01:59.634 --> 00:02:06.380
As for Peter, before he flew away, he saw Wendy once more.

22
00:02:06.381 --> 00:02:13.272
She called to him from the nursery, and he shyly brushed up against the window.

23
00:02:13.273 --> 00:02:17.573
"Peter, are you really going away?" she asked.

24
00:02:17.574 --> 00:02:22.068
"Yes, Wendy. It's time for me to go," he said.

25
00:02:22.069 --> 00:02:27.786
"Peter, don't you want to ask my parents something?" Wendy asked.

26
00:02:27.787 --> 00:02:33.665
"No, what would I ask?" he answered, trying to sound casual.

27
00:02:33.666 --> 00:02:36.476
Mrs. Darling joined them at the window.

28
00:02:36.477 --> 00:02:41.957
When she saw Peter, she told him she would be happy to adopt him as well.

29
00:02:41.958 --> 00:02:46.539
"Would you send me to school?" he asked.

30
00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:48.018
"Yes."

31
00:02:48.019 --> 00:02:50.101
"And then to work?"

32
00:02:50.102 --> 00:02:52.079
"I suppose so."

33
00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:56.342
"Soon I would become a grown-up?" he asked.

34
00:02:56.343 --> 00:02:59.789
"Very soon," said Mrs. Darling.

35
00:02:59.790 --> 00:03:04.589
"I don't want to go to school, and I don't want to be a grown-up—ever!"

36
00:03:04.590 --> 00:03:10.436
Peter protested. "No one is going to catch me and make me grow up."

37
00:03:10.437 --> 00:03:15.677
"But where will you live?" asked Mrs. Darling gently.

38
00:03:15.678 --> 00:03:19.111
"With Tink, in the house we built for Wendy.

39
00:03:19.112 --> 00:03:22.744
The fairies will put it up high among the treetops."

40
00:03:22.745 --> 00:03:26.925
"How lovely," said Wendy longingly.

41
00:03:26.926 --> 00:03:31.154
"I thought all the fairies were dead," said Mrs. Darling.

42
00:03:31.155 --> 00:03:37.477
"There are always more young ones," explained Wendy, who was now an expert on fairies.

43
00:03:37.478 --> 00:03:42.411
"I shall have such fun!" said Peter to Wendy.

44
00:03:42.412 --> 00:03:48.934
"But it will be so lonely in the evenings sitting by the fire," Wendy said sadly.

45
00:03:48.935 --> 00:03:52.562
"Well then, come with me," he said.

46
00:03:52.563 --> 00:03:55.689
"May I, Mother?" Wendy asked.

47
00:03:55.690 --> 00:03:59.522
"Certainly not," Mrs. Darling replied.

48
00:03:59.523 --> 00:04:03.341
"You are finally home, and that is where you will stay."

49
00:04:03.342 --> 00:04:09.123
"But who will look after Peter, and cook and clean for him?" Wendy asked.

50
00:04:09.124 --> 00:04:13.049
"He does so need a mother."

51
00:04:13.050 --> 00:04:17.613
"So do you, Wendy," said her mother sternly.

52
00:04:17.614 --> 00:04:22.266
But when she saw Peter's mouth tremble, she made him another offer.

53
00:04:22.267 --> 00:04:28.094
She would let Wendy join him for one week every year to help him with his spring cleaning.

54
00:04:28.095 --> 00:04:33.031
Having no sense of time, Peter was very happy with this offer.

55
00:04:33.032 --> 00:04:37.523
But Wendy said sadly, "You won't forget me, Peter, will you?

56
00:04:37.524 --> 00:04:40.667
Before spring cleaning time comes?"

57
00:04:40.668 --> 00:04:43.055
Peter promised to remember her.

58
00:04:43.056 --> 00:04:51.648
And then, in the blink of an eye, he flew away.
